{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Ātuma","html":"<article id='thag1.72'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Theragāthā 1.72 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Monks 1.72 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Aṭṭhamavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Chapter Eight </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Ātumattheragāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Ātuma </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Yathā kaḷīro susu vaḍḍhitaggo, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>A young bamboo is hard to extract </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Dunnikkhamo hoti pasākhajāto; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>when the point is grown and become all woody. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Evaṁ ahaṁ bhariyāyānitāya, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>That’s how I feel with the wife <j>who was arranged for me. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Anumaññaṁ maṁ pabbajitomhi dānī”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Give me permission—now I’ve gone forth. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Ātumo thero …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
